From 40f2b0a958744f1c9d624ac2bcbe4723accb04f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:46:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Close custody, MCP secrets, credit-vault and external-signer
 gaps under the local verifier

Custody v2 (CLI custody, MCP secrets) no longer refuses under --chain-verifier /
chainVerifier: custodyChainClients hands custody's own quorum reader ONE
verifier-backed client (network/verified-chain.mjs verifierClient: proof-backed
state pinned to a block hash, headers by number, nothing else) with minAgree 1, so
custody keeps its confirmations, freshness, re-check and rollback rules and never
reads the transaction transport. A custody write's outcome is its exact read-back
in verified state.

The credit-vault CLI takes --chain-verifier: every state read and simulation from
the verifier (verifiedCreditReader); --rpc becomes the optional transaction/history
transport, which never answers state. Outcomes say which parts are verified (the
vault nonce) and which are transport claims (which transaction executed). mint
checks its effect (the vault's code) in verified state.

Sends under the verifier (sendQuorumTx, the external signer's sign, wallet-send,
handoff/attach and rebroadcast paths) wait until verified state reaches the
transport's receipt block and shows the sender's nonce consumed before ANY verdict,
success or revert (VerifiedChain.verifyOutcome), and refuse a transport-supplied
pending nonce that verified state already shows used (assertNonceUnused). A
fabricated receipt therefore leaves the outcome unknown. The signer journals
"nonce-consumed" (terminal: no replay, no resend), and "confirmed" only when the
caller's effect check passed through verified reads. The receipt's contents,
inclusion and status stay labelled UNVERIFIED until a verified receipt source (E)
exists. Legacy (provider quorum) behaviour and wording are unchanged.

Also: the external signer accepts a signature whose zero-valued fields (a zero
priority fee) are RLP-empty and omitted by the parser; the canonical re-encoding
check still requires exactly the prepared bytes.

Tests: test/consumer-closure.test.mjs (offline stand-ins) and
test/consumer-closure.e2e.test.mjs (reth --dev + patched Helios: custody CLI on the
real pinned vault, MCP secrets on the original book-bound vault with a book admin
migration, credit-vault CLI on the production factory fixture, external signer with
lying transports, tampered and missing proofs).
